  "question": {
    "text": "All the students of a class performed poorly in Mathematics. The teacher decided to give grace marks of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> to each of the students. Which of the following statistical measures will not change even after the grace marks were given ?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "0YOgi",
      "text": "mode",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Ger9Z",
      "text": "variance",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "rmXAm",
      "text": "mean",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jLAEX",
      "text": "median",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As we know that with the change in origin, the variance does not change.<p>Therefore, variance does not change even after giving grace marks of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> to each of the students.</p><p>Whereas, mean, mode and median changes upon changing the origin.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
